Which of the following statements are true?
$$\begin{array}{ll}
        \text{I.} & \text{The equation } x^3 + y^3 = 2029 \text{ has no integer solutions.} \\
        \text{II.} & \text{The equation } x^2 + y^2 = 2027 \text{ has no integer solutions.} \\
        \text{III.} & \text{The equation } x^3 + y^3 = 1027 \text{ has no integer solutions.}
        \end{array}$$ Hint: consider remainders.

Let $I$ be an interval of real numbers, and let $f$ be a continuous function defined on $I$ such that $f(x) \in I$ for all $x \in I$ (we say $f$ maps $I$ into itself). A number $c \in I$ is called a fixed point of $f$ if $f(c) = c$.

Consider the following statements:

$
\begin{array}{ll}
\text{I.} & \text{If } I = [0,1] \text{, then } f \text{ has at least one fixed point.} \\
\text{II.} & \text{If } I = (0,1) \text{, then } f \text{ has at least one fixed point.} \\
\text{III.} & \text{If } I = [0,1] \text{ and } f \text{ is strictly decreasing, then } f \text{ has exactly one fixed point.}
\end{array}
$
Which of these must be true?
